016051271327,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":72.5,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0248321509507774,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":30.1,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.021249685731616334,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.017183138155189903,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":71.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003505389536412234,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.21370001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Red River Bancshares, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for Red River Bank that provides banking products and services to commercial and retail customers in the United States. The company offers various deposit products, including checking, saving, money market accounts, and time deposits. It provides commercial real estate loans; one-to-four family mortgage loans and home equity lines of credit; construction and development loans; commercial and industrial loans; small business administration paycheck protection program loans; tax-exempt loans; consumer loans to individuals for personal, family, and household purposes, including secured and unsecured installment and term loans; home mortgage loans; and lines of credit and standby letters of credit. In addition, the company offers treasury management, private banking, and brokerage; investment advisory, financial planning, and a suite of retirement plans; debit and credit cards, direct deposits, cashier's checks, and wire transfer services; online banking services, including access to account balances, online transfers, online bill payment, and electronic delivery of customer statements; and banking services in person, through ATMs, drive-through facilities, night deposits, telephone, mail, mobile banking, and remote deposits. Red River Bancshares, Inc. was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Alexandria, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ronald Blake Chatelain | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $989,207 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 390 people. Revenue per employee of $322K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $108K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Red River Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $689M market cap on $126M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 42% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 35-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 21% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.23290717065036215},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 49% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in RRBI Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_RRBI_Response_111326091201_1794579121.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Red River Bancshares (NASDAQ:RRBI) Sets New 1-Year High \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/red-river-bancshares-nasdaqrrbi-sets-new-1-year-high-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794063693.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (RRBI) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_RRBI_Price_Events_110326092802_1793716082.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793716082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Red River Bancshares (RRBI) Q3 Earnings: Taking a Look at Key Metrics Versus Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3019745/red-river-bancshares-rrbi-q3-earnings-taking-a-look-at-key-metrics-versus-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3019745","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793367002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Red River Bancshares (RRBI) Q3 Earnings and Revenues Top Estimat